> what is the value of i?
  ucas: i
i
> what is the value of pi?
  ucas: pi
3.14159
> what is the range of x plus 1 for a byte x?
  note: "byte" without signed or unsigned: read as unsigned, u8, not signed, i8 (say "unsigned byte", or "assume bytes are signed")
  ucas: it(x: u8) = x + 1
  ucas: range it
range of it -> u8:
  0..255   (256 distinct values)
  fits in u8
  over all 256 points of the domain
> what is the range of x plus 1 for an unsigned byte x?
  ucas: it(x: u8) = x + 1
  ucas: range it
range of it -> u8:
  0..255   (256 distinct values)
  fits in u8
  over all 256 points of the domain
> what is the range of x plus 1 for a signed byte x?
  ucas: it(x: i8) = x + 1
  ucas: range it
range of it -> i8:
  -128..127   (256 distinct values)
  fits in i8
  over all 256 points of the domain
> what is the range of i squared for an integer i?
  note: "integer" without a width: read as an unbounded integer, int, not a C int, i32 (say "32-bit integer", or "assume integers are 32-bit")
  ucas: it(i: int) = i^2
  ucas: range it
range of it -> int:
  0..4
  fits in u3
  undefined at 65532 points
  sampled 65536 points (domain has 2^64 or more points); not exhaustive
> what is the range of i squared for a real i?
  ucas: it(i: real) = i^2
  ucas: range it
range of it:
  [0, 100]   min at i ≈ 0, max at i ≈ -10
  grid of 20001 points over [-10, 10] (default; give x a range), extrema refined at critical points
